WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:08.519
We are a nation under God, and I believe God
intended for us to be free. We must realize

00:00:08.519 --> 00:00:15.070
that no arsenal or no weapon in the arsenals
of the world is so formidable as the will

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:23.410
and moral courage of free men and women. The
price for this freedom at times has been high,

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:31.020
but we have never been unwilling to pay that
price. Those who say that we’re in a time when

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:39.129
there are no heroes, they just don’t know
where to look. The sloping hills of Arlington

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:49.300
National Cemetery with its row upon row of
simple white markers bearing crosses or stars of David.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:58.829
Their lives ended in places called Belleau
Wood, The Argonne, Omaha Beach, Salerno, and

00:00:58.829 --> 00:01:06.619
halfway around the world on Guadalcanal, Tarawa,
Pork Chop Hill, the Chosin Reservoir, and

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:14.060
in a hundred rice paddies and jungles of a
place called Vietnam. They add up to only

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:20.760
a tiny fraction of the price that has been
paid for our freedom.

00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:42.640
To fallen soldiers let us sing
Where no rockets fly nor bullets wing

00:01:42.640 --> 00:02:00.780
Our broken brothers let us bring
To the Mansions of the Lord

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:19.940
No more bleeding, no more fight
No prayers pleading through the night

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:39.120
Just divine embrace, eternal light
In the Mansions of the Lord.

00:02:39.120 --> 00:03:00.880
Where no mothers cry and no children weep
We will stand and guard though the angels sleep

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:23.020
Through the ages safely keep
The Mansions of the Lord.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:37.500
Ready. Aim. Fire

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:41.820
Ready. Present arms.

